 col←readListColumn(vector data row_count);child_vector;child_type;child_type_id;child_data;entries;offsets;lengths;i;list_entry;child_count;child_col
⍝ Read a LIST column from a DuckDB vector
⍝ vector: the DuckDB vector pointer
⍝ data: pointer to the list entry data
⍝ row_count: number of rows
⍝ Returns: vector of APL arrays (one per list)

⎕io←0

⍝ Get the child vector (contains the actual list elements)
child_vector←api.duckdb_list_vector_get_child vector

⍝ Get child vector info
child_type←api.duckdb_vector_get_column_type child_vector
child_type_id←api.duckdb_get_type_id child_type
child_data←api.duckdb_vector_get_data child_vector

⍝ Read list entries (offset and length pairs)
⍝ Each entry is 16 bytes: offset (8 bytes) + length (8 bytes)
entries←(row_count×2)read.u64 data
offsets←entries[2×⍳row_count]
lengths←entries[1+2×⍳row_count]

⍝ Read all child elements at once based on child type
child_count←api.duckdb_list_vector_get_size vector
child_col←readChildElements child_vector child_type_id child_data child_count

⍝ Build the result: each row gets a list of its elements
col←{
    offset←offsets[⍵]
    length←lengths[⍵]
    0=length:⍬  ⍝ Empty list
    child_col[offset+⍳length]  ⍝ Extract elements for this row
}¨⍳row_count

⍝ KSL 2.0.0
